+
+    Entry::request_cleanup closes its mailbox and waits for drained() before
+    publishing cleanup. Mailbox cancellation publishes the retained Response
+    and clears its call without a dying Linux worker's userspace RET log.
+    Thus this real successful cleanup ACK proves that exact Entry's admitted
+    poll drained. No worker-retired row or retirement0 is invented: query -11
+    may remain until the parent performs the real wait/destructor transaction.
+    """
+    ordered=sorted(children,key=children.get)
+    _need(len(ordered)==2 and child==ordered[0] and len(missing)==1 and len(terminals)==1,
+          "cancelled child/one-poll scope")
+    key=next(iter(missing));terminal_key=next(iter(terminals))
+    delivered=groups[child]["delivered"]
+    (cpu,number),begin=delivered[key];(tcpu,tnumber),terminal=delivered[terminal_key]
+    _need(cpu==tcpu==0 and number==7 and tnumber==231 and key[0]!=terminal_key[0] and begin<terminal,
+          "cancelled poll/other-worker terminal")
+    _need(all(k==key or k[0]!=key[0] or pos<begin for k,(_,pos) in delivered.items()),
+          "cancelled worker reused after poll")
+    parent=int(re.fullmatch(r"os=\d+ generation=\d+ pid=(\d+)",prefix).group(1))
